 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "I would like...",
     "texto": [
      "**Хотел бы** («I would like») softens the desire compared with **хочу** («I want»): **Я бы хотел поехать в Москву** («I would like to go to Moscow»). The past form agrees with the speaker: a man says **я бы хотел** and a woman says **я бы хотела**.",
      "With **мочь** you also use **мог/могла бы + infinitive**. The form agrees with the subject: **Мог бы ты помочь?** is addressed to a man; **Могла бы ты помочь?** to a woman. After **хотеть** and **мочь** comes the infinitive: **Я бы хотела отдохнуть** («I would like to rest»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Advice",
     "texto": [
      "To give advice: **на твоём месте** («in your place») + **я бы** + past; the verb agrees with the speaker. **На твоём месте я бы поехала летом**: «In your place, I would go in the summer» (said by a woman).",
      "**Лучше бы + past** can express a recommendation, a wish or regret; the context clarifies the nuance. With a reference to the past: **Лучше бы ты вчера отдохнул** («It would have been better if you had rested yesterday»). To advise what to do now or later you can also say **На твоём месте я бы…**, or use the more formal recommendation **следует + infinitive**: **Следует отдохнуть** («it is advisable to rest / one should rest»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
